      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clock) (count == $countones(busy)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "This invariant relates the counter to the actual number of occupied entries. It holds initially because count and every busy bit are zero. Assuming it holds before a transition, an accepted allocation selects an unoccupied entry and increases both quantities by one. An effective free clears an occupied entry and decreases both quantities by one. When both operations occur, their effective addresses are distinct because allocation selects an entry that was unoccupied, so their changes cancel. At zero occupancy, no free can decrement count; at full occupancy, nack blocks allocation. Thus the invariant is preserved by one transition and implies count <= SIZE, making the strengthened target 1-inductive. This argument applies to the supplied default parameters, for which every entry has a representable address."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

